  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 940 PM MDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nUNSEASONABLY WARM AND MOSTLY DRY THROUGH THE WEEKEND: \n\nWith high pressure in place across the Southwest, warm and dry \nconditions will be favored through the weekend. Temperatures \nwill range from 5 to 15 degrees above normal across the region.\nA mild boost in moisture Sunday afternoon could lead to \nisolated convection over the San Juans, but without much else \ndriving active weather, the vast majority of the region should \nanticipate a dry weekend.\n\nWORK WEEK OUTLOOK: \n\nLooking ahead to next week, high pressure breaks down late \nMonday into Tuesday as a shortwave trough advects through the \nnorthwesterly flow. This could again prompt terrain-based\nshowers, but with dry surface levels in place, measurable \nrainfall could be hard to come by. Beyond this weak disturbance,\nhigh pressure and warm and dry conditions remain the name of \nthe game through the work week.",
